name: requirements-traceability
-- specs/business-rules/retention.business-rule.spec.md --
---
type: business-rule-spec
---
# Recovery window

## Statement

Workspace members may recover accidentally deleted documents during the 30 days following deletion.

## Supports

[Reduce lost work](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#reduce-lost-work).

## Rationale

The organization commits to a bounded recovery period. This business rule does not itself specify the storage implementation.

## Applies to

**Targets:** [Document workspace](../document-workspace.system.spec.md)

Applies to workspace members and documents deleted within that workspace.

## Authority

The workspace team's recovery policy establishes this example rule.
-- specs/concepts/trash.concept.spec.md --
---
type: concept-spec
---
# Trash

## Purpose

Make deletion reversible until a retained item expires.

## Operational principles

If an item is deleted and then restored before it expires, it becomes available again with its retained content.

## State

Items are either available, retained after deletion, or expired.

## Actions

### Delete

Move an available item into retained state with its deletion time.

### Restore

Move a retained, unexpired item into available state.

### Expire

Remove an expired item from retained state.
-- specs/jobs/recover.job.spec.md --
---
type: job-spec
---
# Recover lost work

## Job

When valuable work is accidentally removed, I want to recover it so I can continue without recreating it.

## Supports

[Reduce lost work](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#reduce-lost-work).

## Outcomes

### Minimize the time required to resume work after

Minimize the time required to resume work after recovering an accidentally deleted document.

## Performer

A workspace member who has accidentally deleted valuable work.
-- specs/requirements/restoration.requirement.spec.md --
---
type: requirement-spec
---
# Preserve document metadata on restoration

## Statement

For the restoration required by Restore retained content, the restored metadata must preserve the original title, author identity, creation time and workspace identity.

## Refines

[Restore retained content](restore-content.requirement.spec.md).

The refinement makes the required metadata explicit without weakening the parent's recovery window or authorization condition.

## Relies on

[Trusted time](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#trusted-time).

## Applies to

**Targets:** [Restore a document](../use-cases/restore.use-case.spec.md), [DocumentTrash](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#documenttrash)

## Rationale

Preserving these metadata fields lets members resume work with the same document identity and attribution. The Refines section identifies the governing requirement.
-- specs/document-workspace.system.spec.md --
---
type: system-spec
---
# Document workspace

## Purpose

Help teams preserve and recover valuable work.

## Scope

Document deletion and restoration within a workspace.

## Goals

### Reduce lost work

Reduce the amount of valuable work lost through accidental deletion.

## Assumptions

### Trusted time

The platform supplies a trustworthy UTC clock for retention calculations.

#### Basis

The hosting agreement names the platform clock as the time source.

#### Applicability

Every retention calculation in the workspace.

## Concept uses

### DocumentTrash

#### Definition

[Trash](concepts/trash.concept.spec.md)

#### Supports

[Recover lost work](jobs/recover.job.spec.md).

#### Relies on

[Trusted time](#trusted-time) bounds retention intervals.
-- specs/use-cases/restore.use-case.spec.md --
---
type: use-case-spec
---
# Restore a document

## Goal

Recover an accidentally deleted document and resume work.

## System boundary

**Subject system:** [Document workspace](../document-workspace.system.spec.md)

The workspace owns retention and restoration; external backups are outside this boundary.

## Supports

[Recover lost work](../jobs/recover.job.spec.md).

## Involves

[DocumentTrash](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#documenttrash).

## Main success scenario

1. The member selects a retained document.
2. The workspace restores it according to [Restore retained content](../requirements/restore-content.requirement.spec.md).
3. The member resumes work.

## Success guarantees

The member can resume work on the restored document.

## Authority

The use case specifies the interaction. [Restore retained content](../requirements/restore-content.requirement.spec.md) specifies the recovery behavior.

## Primary actor

An authorized workspace member.

## Goal level

User task.

## Sequence

The scenario order is representative; the recovery requirement governs restoration.

## Extensions

### The recovery deadline has passed

The workspace declines restoration from retained state and explains that the recovery window has ended.

### The member lacks authorization

The workspace declines restoration and leaves the retained document unchanged.

-- specs/requirements/restore-content.requirement.spec.md --
---
type: requirement-spec
id: restore-content
---
# Restore retained content

## Statement

When an authorized workspace member requests restoration before the 30-day recovery period ends, the workspace must restore the retained document content and metadata.

## Derived from

[Recovery window](../business-rules/retention.business-rule.spec.md) supplies the time boundary.

## Supports

[Recover lost work](../jobs/recover.job.spec.md).

## Applies to

**Targets:** [DocumentTrash](../document-workspace.system.spec.md#documenttrash)

## Rationale

Restoration lets members resume work with the document they retained.
